Aerie-Purpose: Give shared workers and service workers the noise tokens of the top-level site of their storage key, and make WebGL and WebGPU in workers follow the per-site and global switches instead of always masking.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: content/browser/helium_noise, content/browser/worker_host, content/browser/service_worker, content/renderer/worker, content/renderer/service_worker, third_party/blink/public/mojom/worker, third_party/blink/public/mojom/service_worker, third_party/blink/public/web, third_party/blink/renderer/core/exported, third_party/blink/renderer/modules/exported
Aerie-Kind: hook

Follows hardening/0013 (issue #113, part of #87). A shared worker or a service worker is started by the browser
for a storage key, not by one page, so the browser derives its tokens:
HeliumNoiseTokenData::GetTokensForWorker(context, storage_key) takes the top-level site of the key
(net::SchemefulSite, the same unit that keys a window's tokens and the per-site switch, so the worker's values
equal its pages' values on the same site, and a third party frame's worker gets its embedder's) and asks the
same ContentBrowserClient::HeliumNoiseEnabled that a navigation asks. When protection is off for the browser or
the site the map is empty and the worker sees the real values. Only derived per-site tokens leave the
browser, never the session tokens.

The tokens travel in a new last argument of SharedWorkerFactory.CreateSharedWorker and a new last field of
EmbeddedWorkerStartParams (a map, empty when off), then through WebSharedWorker::CreateAndStart and
WebEmbeddedWorkerStartData into GlobalScopeCreationParams::helium_noise_tokens (hardening/0013). A service
worker's tokens are worked out each time it starts, so a change of the switch applies at its next start. A
shared worker is created per connection set, so a change applies to a worker started after it.

With tokens in every worker, ShouldMaskGpuInfoForContext (hardening/0010) no longer treats a worker as always
masked: a window or a worker follows its kWebGL token, and only a null context stays fail closed. The test
mock of the shared worker factory takes the new argument.

